# Original practice material. These are teaching tasks, not official exam items.
READING = [
 {"id":"R1","title":"Simulated companions and autonomy","vi_title":"Bạn đồng hành mô phỏng và quyền tự chủ",
  "text":"A simulated companion may reduce loneliness, but benefit alone does not settle the ethical question. The first issue is whether the user understands the system’s limits. A model that appears to remember, care and choose can encourage attachment even when it has no independent interests. The second issue is design incentive. If a platform profits from prolonged engagement, it may optimise for dependency rather than wellbeing. A useful safeguard is therefore not merely a warning label; it is a set of testable design constraints. The system should disclose its nature, avoid impersonating real persons without consent, and provide friction that encourages breaks. It should also allow users to export or delete interaction histories. Critics may argue that such rules treat adults as children. Yet transparency does not remove choice; it makes choice informed. The strongest position is neither prohibition nor uncritical acceptance. It is a demand that comfort be compatible with autonomy.",
  "questions":[("What is the main claim?","Luận điểm chính là gì?",["Simulated companions should be banned.","Comfort must be compatible with autonomy.","Users cannot understand warnings.","Platforms always optimise wellbeing."],1,"The final sentence states the balanced position.","Câu cuối nêu lập trường cân bằng."),("Why does the author mention profit?","Vì sao tác giả nhắc lợi nhuận?",["To praise platform business models.","To identify a possible conflict of interest.","To prove all users are lonely.","To explain memory storage."],1,"Profit can reward dependency rather than wellbeing.","Lợi nhuận có thể thưởng cho phụ thuộc thay vì hạnh phúc."),("Which safeguard is NOT listed?","Biện pháp nào KHÔNG được liệt kê?",["Disclosing the system’s nature.","Exporting interaction histories.","Mandatory daily medication.","Encouraging breaks."],2,"Medication is not part of the passage.","Thuốc không nằm trong đoạn văn."),("The word friction most nearly means","Từ friction gần nghĩa nhất với",["deliberate pauses or obstacles","physical violence","software errors","legal punishment"],0,"Friction here means design features that interrupt automatic use.","Friction ở đây là đặc điểm thiết kế ngắt việc dùng tự động."),("What is the author’s tone toward critics?","Giọng điệu với người phê phán là gì?",["Dismissive and mocking.","Engaged but disagreeing.","Completely agreeing.","Indifferent."],1,"The author answers the objection rather than ignoring it.","Tác giả trả lời phản đối thay vì phớt lờ.")],
  "vi_summary":"Đoạn văn lập luận rằng bạn đồng hành mô phỏng chỉ hợp đạo đức khi sự an ủi tương thích với quyền tự chủ: minh bạch, không giả mạo người thật, có ngắt quãng và cho phép xuất/xóa lịch sử."},
 {"id":"R2","title":"Closed habitats and resource accounting","vi_title":"Môi trường khép kín và hạch toán tài nguyên",
  "text":"A habitat is often described as closed when its air and water are recycled. That description is useful but incomplete. Closure is a matter of degree and of boundaries. A station may recycle water efficiently while importing food, soil nutrients and replacement parts. It may also export waste heat or depend on external energy. A more honest account asks what crosses the boundary, how often, and what happens if the supply stops. Engineers therefore distinguish between recycling loops and true self-sufficiency. The difference matters politically as well as technically. A community that controls its loops can negotiate from strength; one that depends on a single supplier can be coerced through maintenance schedules. None of this implies that openness is bad. Trade can increase resilience by diversifying sources. The key question is whether dependencies are visible, redundant and governed by fair rules.",
  "questions":[("What is the passage primarily about?","Đoạn văn chủ yếu bàn gì?",["How to build a water filter.","How to evaluate habitat closure and dependency.","Why trade should stop.","How to export waste heat."],1,"The passage reframes closure as boundary accounting.","Đoạn văn định khung lại tính khép kín như hạch toán ranh giới."),("According to the text, a station may recycle water but still","Theo đoạn văn, một trạm có thể tái chế nước nhưng vẫn",["be fully self-sufficient","import food and parts","produce no waste heat","avoid all external energy"],1,"The second and third sentences give this example.","Câu hai và ba nêu ví dụ này."),("Why does maintenance matter politically?","Vì sao bảo trì quan trọng về chính trị?",["It always lowers prices.","A supplier can use it as leverage.","It removes all boundaries.","It makes recycling unnecessary."],1,"Dependency on one supplier enables coercion.","Phụ thuộc một nhà cung cấp cho phép ép buộc."),("The author’s view of trade is","Quan điểm tác giả về thương mại là",["wholly negative","conditionally positive","unexamined","hostile to diversity"],1,"Trade can help if dependencies are visible and fair.","Thương mại có ích nếu phụ thuộc minh bạch và công bằng."),("Which question best extends the argument?","Câu hỏi nào mở rộng lập luận tốt nhất?",["What colour are the pipes?","Who governs the boundary dependencies?","How many tourists visit?","Which brand is popular?"],1,"Governance is the passage’s final criterion.","Quản trị là tiêu chí cuối của đoạn văn.")],
  "vi_summary":"Đoạn văn phân biệt vòng tái chế với tự cung tự cấp, nhấn mạnh rằng phụ thuộc phải minh bạch, có dự phòng và được quản trị công bằng."},
 {"id":"R3","title":"Recorded labour and consent","vi_title":"Lao động được ghi lại và đồng thuận",
  "text":"When a worker’s actions are recorded, the recording can outlive the original shift. This creates a gap between consent to perform and consent to reuse. A person may agree to be filmed for training yet not agree to synthetic replay in advertising. The distinction is not merely legal; it concerns control over one’s social presence. A reasonable framework would specify purpose, duration, audience and revocation. It would also recognise that bargaining power is unequal. A freelancer who needs income may accept terms that a salaried professional could refuse. For that reason, consent should be treated as an ongoing relationship rather than a single signature. Platforms can help by making reuse visible and by providing simple withdrawal mechanisms. The goal is not to prevent all recording, but to prevent a person’s past from being turned into an unlimited resource.",
  "questions":[("What gap does the passage identify?","Đoạn văn chỉ ra khoảng trống nào?",["Between filming and storage hardware.","Between consent to perform and consent to reuse.","Between salary and freelance work.","Between training and advertising law only."],1,"The second sentence names the central gap.","Câu hai gọi tên khoảng trống trung tâm."),("Which element is NOT part of the proposed framework?","Yếu tố nào KHÔNG thuộc khung đề xuất?",["Purpose","Duration","Audience","Unlimited sublicensing"],3,"Unlimited sublicensing contradicts the argument.","Cấp phép lại vô hạn trái lập luận."),("Why is bargaining power relevant?","Vì sao quyền thương lượng liên quan?",["It makes all contracts invalid.","It can make formal consent less free.","It removes the need for rules.","It guarantees fair pay."],1,"Economic pressure can constrain real choice.","Áp lực kinh tế có thể hạn chế lựa chọn thực."),("Ongoing relationship suggests consent should be","Quan hệ đang tiếp diễn gợi ý đồng thuận nên",["permanent and irreversible","revisitable and withdrawable","signed only once","ignored after payment"],1,"Revocation and withdrawal are emphasised.","Thu hồi và rút lui được nhấn mạnh."),("The final sentence implies that","Câu cuối hàm ý rằng",["all recording is harmful","past labour should not become an unlimited resource","workers dislike technology","platforms cannot help"],1,"The goal is bounded reuse, not prohibition.","Mục tiêu là tái sử dụng có giới hạn, không phải cấm.")],
  "vi_summary":"Đoạn văn đề xuất khung đồng thuận cho lao động được ghi: mục đích, thời hạn, khán giả, quyền thu hồi và cơ chế rút lui đơn giản."},
]
LISTENING = [
 {"id":"L1","title":"Why summaries fail","vi_title":"Vì sao tóm tắt thất bại",
  "script":"Good morning. Today I want to challenge a common study habit. Many students summarise by copying the first sentence of each paragraph. That produces a list, not an argument. A better summary identifies the claim, the supporting move and the limitation. Suppose a passage says that remote work increases flexibility but weakens informal mentoring. A weak summary says remote work has advantages and disadvantages. A strong summary says the author accepts flexibility gains while arguing that unplanned learning suffers. Notice the difference: the strong version preserves the relationship between ideas. To practise, read a short paragraph, close it, and write one sentence beginning although or while. Then check whether your sentence keeps the contrast. If it does not, you probably collected topics instead of structure.",
  "questions":[("What habit is criticised?","Thói quen nào bị phê phán?",["Copying first sentences.","Writing one sentence.","Using although.","Closing the book."],0),("What does a strong summary preserve?","Tóm tắt mạnh giữ được gì?",["Every example.","The relationship between ideas.","The first sentence only.","The author’s biography."],1),("Which opening words are recommended?","Từ mở đầu nào được khuyên?",["Because and so.","Although or while.","First and finally.","In addition and also."],1),("What is the speaker’s purpose?","Mục đích người nói là gì?",["To advertise a course.","To teach a summary technique.","To reject remote work.","To explain mentoring law."],1)],
  "vi_summary":"Bài nói gốc hướng dẫn tóm tắt bằng cấu trúc lập luận: nhượng bộ, luận điểm và giới hạn, thay vì chép câu đầu."},
 {"id":"L2","title":"Observation and interpretation","vi_title":"Quan sát và diễn giải",
  "script":"In fieldwork, students often mix what they saw with what they concluded. Imagine you observe a person checking a door three times. The observation is the repeated action. The interpretation might be anxiety, habit or a faulty lock. You cannot decide from the action alone. A useful note therefore has two columns: observation and possible explanation. The second column should remain open until more evidence arrives. This discipline matters in language learning too. When you hear an unfamiliar phrase, write the sounds you noticed before guessing the meaning. Separating levels reduces premature certainty. It also makes your later correction easier, because you can see exactly where the inference entered.",
  "questions":[("What is the observation in the example?","Quan sát trong ví dụ là gì?",["The person is anxious.","The lock is faulty.","The door is checked three times.","The habit is strange."],2),("What should the second column contain?","Cột thứ hai nên chứa gì?",["Only facts.","Possible explanations.","Final judgments.","Unrelated vocabulary."],1),("Why separate levels?","Vì sao tách các mức?",["To avoid all inference.","To reduce premature certainty.","To make notes longer.","To remove evidence."],1),("What language-learning example is given?","Ví dụ học ngôn ngữ nào được nêu?",["Writing an essay.","Hearing an unfamiliar phrase.","Reading a novel aloud.","Memorising a word list."],1)],
  "vi_summary":"Bài nói gốc phân biệt quan sát với diễn giải và đề xuất ghi chú hai cột để tránh chắc chắn quá sớm."},
]
